From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 06:22:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] EncodingHelper: route hardware accel selection through
 decode/encode accessors

HardwareAccelerationType decides both which decoder and which encoder a
transcode uses, and EncodingHelper reads it in places that want different
answers. A platform whose best decoder and best encoder come from different
stacks cannot be described: it has to pick one and lose the other, or smuggle
the pairing inside a type whose name only names one half.

Introduce GetDecodeType() and GetEncodeType() and route every read through
whichever one that site means. Both return HardwareAccelerationType, so this
commit changes no behaviour whatsoever -- it is the classification, separated
out so it can be reviewed on its own before anything depends on it.

The classification, for review:

  encode  GetH26xOrAv1Encoder, GetMjpegEncoder -- codecMap and _mjpegCodecMap
          pick the encoder binary; GetVideoQualityParam -- every branch appends
          to the encoder parameter string (-low_power, -async_depth).

  decode  GetHwaccelType and GetHardwareVideoDecoder with the bit-depth and
          profile gates in front of them; the six Get*VidDecoder guards;
          GetHwDecoderName; GetInputVideoHwaccelArgs; and GetInputModifier's
          input demuxer hint, which is an input-side decision.

  decode  the filter chain: GetVideoProcessingFilterParam's dispatch and the
          six Get*VidFilterChain guards that mirror it, plus
          IsIntelVppTonemapAvailable. The chain has to accept the surface the
          decoder produced, so it follows the decoder.

MediaEncoder's keyframe-only extraction check and the VideoToolbox
low-priority decode flag are decode. Its VA-API device probe is neither: it
inspects the device that either half would use, so it now asks about both.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../MediaEncoding/EncodingHelper.cs           | 66 ++++++++++++-------
 .../Encoder/MediaEncoder.cs                   |  7 +-
